    "title": "Here are some tips to avoid donation scams this holiday season - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By John Gregory ,\n8 hours ago\nThere's a charity and a cause for just about everything, and it's never been easier to give - that's what scammers are counting on.\nProtecting yourself against scammers means doing your homework, and there are websites that can actually help.\nCharity Watch, Charity Navigator, Guide Star and the Better Business Bureau Wise Giving Alliance offer ratings about different charities.\nDon't allow yourself to be pressured by unsolicited calls.\nAnd if you make a donation online, make sure the URL begins with \"https.\" That ensures the website is secure.\nIt's also encouraged that you record your donation and make sure it corresponds with your financial statements.\nAlso be careful you don't accidentally sign up for recurring donations, which some charities sneak in.\nIt can be daunting, and in the end, it may make sense to stick with charities you know and trust.",
